class PaperLineageIn(BaseModel):
    """
    Where this paper came from, answered AT ADD TIME (0180).

    THE PRESENCE OF THIS OBJECT IS THE ANSWER "I LOOKED". That is the whole
    design of the tri-state, expressed on the wire:

      lineage omitted          -> papers.lineage_state stays NULL = UNKNOWN.
                                  Nobody asked. Every client that predates this
                                  field lands here for free, with no version
                                  negotiation and no capability probe.
      lineage: {"via": null}   -> 'none'. The agent looked and there was no
                                  parent: a bare search, or a human handing over
                                  a link. A POSITIVE claim, and the reason
                                  omission and this cannot be the same shape.
      lineage: {"via": "<id>"} -> an edge, and 'declared'.

    WHY CAPTURED HERE AND NOT RECONSTRUCTED LATER. When the agent calls
    `paper add`, "how I got here" is two turns back in its own context and
    verifiable. Ten papers and one compaction later it is guessing. The same
    information has completely different reliability depending only on when you
    ask for it -- and the server cannot ask on its own behalf, because a
    `find_papers` read leaves no trace it could join against (the only record is
    a counts-only analytics event whose stated contract is "counts, never
    content", and the search endpoint writes nothing to the database at all).
    """

    provenance: PaperProvenance | None = None
    reason: Reason | None = Field(None, title='Reason')
    via: UUID | None = Field(None, title='Via')


